  "id": "u10-tackle-secure-go-again-v082",
  "title": "U10 | Tackle, secure and go again",
  "age": "U10",
  "category": "Attack",
  "length": 20,
  "width": 15,
  "objective": "Retain possession after a tackle: present the ball, recognise the first defender at the breakdown, support from the correct side and move the ball into space for a second phase.",
  "safety": "Coach-led, age-appropriate progression only. First rehearse at walking pace with touch or no-contact representation; progress to controlled contact only when qualified coaching and player readiness allow. Check surface, space, equipment, club guidance and consent/readiness. Use the shield as a passive visual or controlled-contact aid only if permitted by the club’s age-grade and safeguarding guidance; never charge into it or through a grounded player. Stop immediately for unsafe head/neck position, loss of balance or pain. No diving, squeeze ball, neck rolls, lifting or hand-offs. U10: original carrier/tackler plus one arriving player per side at the breakdown; when the ball is secured, use it within five seconds of the referee’s call. No hands in a formed ruck for the arriving player in this scenario. After the second tackle, release and present before reset.",
